# Model routing (RealmsRPG)

**Never** a slug ending in `-fast`. Pass the standard slug. Fast is the product default.

`composer-2.5` is the **default whenever possible**, including small UI, copy, labels, straightforward bug, mechanical edit of an approved plan, and a **local save or input fix** whose expected behavior is already written. A save, click handler, or field parse does **not** by itself leave Composer. Step up only when Composer cannot do the task well.

| Work | Slug |
|------|------|
| Default, including local save or input fix with behavior already written | `composer-2.5` |
| Bug that crosses systems — daily problem-solving | `grok-4.7-medium` |
| Rules math, missing written rule, Supabase, RLS, schema, migrations, architecture | `grok-4.7-high` |
| Only after High has failed on that problem — note it on the task | `grok-4.7-xhigh` |

**Do not start** Claude, GPT, or any Other Models slug. Comment the recommendation (`claude-opus-5-5-high` or `gpt-5.6-sol-high`) on the ClickUp task and leave the task **to do** (no branch) or **in progress** (branch exists) for Kadin to approve.

**Audit:** use a **different** model from the implementer chat — see `.cursor/commands/audit.md` (read-only; never `-fast`).
